WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
- One of the best feelings
in the entire world is

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.180
the feeling of getting better

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.350
at the things that you're interested in.

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.460
If you're starting to get into the gym,

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:09.610
it feels really good

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:12.650
to actually see yourself getting stronger.

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.980
Whether that's visually,

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.670
or the fact that you
can bench more pounds.

00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:18.820
Getting stronger and hitting new records

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.190
is at least half the fun

00:00:20.190 --> 00:00:22.670
if not all the fun of going to the gym.

00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:23.950
If you're a piano player

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:27.680
and you've been practicing
your improvisational skills,

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.610
it feels really good

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.970
to be able to just make
a banger of a melody

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:32.610
in like five minutes.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.320
It feels good to walk around life

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.480
with a certain level of competence.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:37.710
You've put in the work,

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.390
you're better at certain
things than most people

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:43.400
competence makes you
more useful to yourself,

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.540
to your family,

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.460
to your community,

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.540
and it kind of makes
the world a better place

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:48.373
if you think about it.

00:00:48.373 --> 00:00:50.010
But if you've spent pretty much any time

00:00:50.010 --> 00:00:51.580
on the internet whatsoever

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.080
you've probably noticed that

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.220
there's a culture that exists on Reddit

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:57.300
and on YouTube,

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:58.950
and on bodybuilding forums

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:00.760
that sees self-improvement

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.170
as its own standalone hobby

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:06.340
detached from any particular
interest or a goal.

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.510
And it's used almost like a

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.700
widely prescribed antidote
for a crappy life.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.200
You feeling down in the dumps,

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.510
try self-improvement.

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.560
Oh damn! your dog died.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:16.990
There's this self-improvement book

00:01:16.990 --> 00:01:17.950
that I heard is really good.

00:01:17.950 --> 00:01:19.300
You should go pick it up and read it.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.290
Damn, that sucks dude,

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:21.230
your wife left you?

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:24.160
There's this bald
self-improvement YouTuber

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.640
that gives really good advice.

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:26.500
You should give him a try.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.730
And that's either a good
thing or a bad thing.

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:31.180
I don't think you can
really bash the sentiment

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.590
because improving yourself

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:36.260
is obviously a noble and worthwhile aim.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.390
Like what else are you gonna do?

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:38.400
Do like get worse?

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.110
But one thing that I
do think is destructive

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:44.090
is that these internet
self-improvement communities

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:47.350
seem to either intentionally
or unintentionally

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:50.430
sell this idea of self-improvement

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.720
kind of being the answer to everything.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.900
They sell this idea

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.670
of being able to improve
yourself to a point

00:01:56.670 --> 00:02:00.330
where you don't really have
to deal with life struggles.

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.780
You can eventually improve yourself

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:02.930
to a point where,

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:04.010
everybody loves you

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:05.610
because you're so charismatic,

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.030
you have such a rocking body,

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:10.530
everyone's just impressed with
your matte DIA Vela biceps,

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.110
I'm not ripping on mat DIA Vela

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.030
those things are huge.

00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:15.430
You'll eventually make so much money that,

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:17.370
you can pretty much buy anything you want.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.430
And all this stuff sounds really great,

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.970
who wouldn't want all that stuff.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.540
But as soon as you say it out loud,

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.170
it becomes pretty clear that

00:02:24.170 --> 00:02:25.360
this type of thinking

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:28.130
almost stems from a place of insecurity

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:29.690
of conditional happiness.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.230
It comes from a certain dissatisfaction

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:33.460
of where you are now.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.210
Self-improvement therefore

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.280
becomes kind of like a vehicle

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:39.730
that will take you towards this fantasy,

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:42.100
this perfect life that
you've always dreamed.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.290
But if you look at some of
the most successful people

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.340
on planet earth,

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:47.900
I can guarantee you they
didn't get to where they were

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.640
by just being really
into self-improvement.

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:51.830
Usually they get there

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:54.240
by being really fricking
good at something.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.790
Bill Gates was obsessed with coding.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.970
Billion Musk, What's he not into.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:00.810
If you look up to these types of people

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.240
and you want to be somewhat like them,

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.560
you have to realize that
they're not obsessing

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.800
over their perfect morning routine

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.040
and figuring out how to
like stack certain vitamins

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.610
so that you can see through walls

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:15.820
and unlock some sort of third
eye of truth or something.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.300
That stuff is useful,

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:18.560
but it's only useful

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.490
if you're already doing something.

00:03:20.490 --> 00:03:22.740
One of the funniest examples of

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:26.470
self-improvement being super
counterproductive or unhelpful

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:30.160
is people who read a lot of
books about social interaction.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.000
And I'm totally not
speaking from experience.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:33.350
It seems like common sense

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.420
that the best way to get
better at socializing

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:37.590
is to socialize.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.940
To go out on a Friday night

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:41.300
instead of spending your
time playing video games.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.160
But there was a point in my life where

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.930
I didn't really socialize at all,

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:47.257
and all I did was read books like

00:03:47.257 --> 00:03:49.580
"How to Win Friends and Influence People"

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:53.830
and "The Likes Switch" and
"Models" by Mark Manson.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.470
And it's almost like I was an alien

00:03:55.470 --> 00:03:58.500
trying to learn how to
socially interact with people

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:00.420
while I was locking myself in my house,

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:02.410
not getting any exposure to people.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:03.860
It's like the perfect example

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.940
of obsessive self-improvement

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.510
not doing anything to help me improve.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.640
The very thing that I
was trying to improve

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:13.490
was being sabotaged by the fact that I was

00:04:13.490 --> 00:04:16.140
cerebralising it, theorizing about it,

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:17.760
instead of just getting out there

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.160
and getting experience.

00:04:19.160 --> 00:04:21.210
Now, the books that I just mentioned

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:24.070
are helpful and I've recommended
them on the channel before,

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.310
but they're only helpful

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:27.650
if the vast majority of your time

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:31.790
is spent out there in the
real world, just living.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.710
If all you watch is
self-improvement videos,

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:37.320
every book you read is
a self-improvement book,

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:39.640
and self-improvement is your main hobby,

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.920
it's almost like you're a
Knight in the middle ages

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.640
and you spend like your entire life

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:46.570
deep within the castle walls,

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:48.480
obsessively sharpening your sword

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.540
and optimizing your equipment,

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:52.900
meanwhile, there's a war raging on

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:54.600
outside the castle walls

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.830
and the kingdom really needs your help,

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.140
maybe the princess got
captured by a dragon

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:00.250
or something like that,

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:02.460
but you're just sitting there inside

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.730
making sure you have like
the perfect equipment

00:05:04.730 --> 00:05:06.540
and you're doing tons of pushups and stuff

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.700
and making sure you're in shape,

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:10.210
but you have no clue

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:12.550
how to fight any of
the monsters out there.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:14.840
You've never been on an adventure before.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.360
So it's like you have the
sharpest sword in the world,

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:19.350
but no idea how to use it.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.540
And you're running out of time.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:23.220
And what most people who
eventually break out of this

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:25.330
self-improvement obsession,

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.810
eventually figure out

00:05:26.810 --> 00:05:28.620
is that it was far better to

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:30.640
hack and slash their way through life

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:31.960
with a dull sword

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:34.970
than to spend your entire
life inside with a sharp one.

00:05:34.970 --> 00:05:36.770
Now it would obviously be pretty stupid

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.820
if you never sharpened your sword.

00:05:38.820 --> 00:05:41.120
If you never picked up a book

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:43.590
that suggested a different
way of doing things,

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:46.040
if you never questioned
your current lifestyle

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:47.560
and what you can do to improve it,

00:05:47.560 --> 00:05:48.940
but get out the door,

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:49.950
go make some mistakes

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.110
go try some things,

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:52.260
go live life,

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.163
and sharpen your sword along the way.

